    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9314" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνοστ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unreturning, without return,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντας ὄλεσαν καὶ ἔθηκαν ἀνόστους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					24.528
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντες ἐγένοντο ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					145
				</span></i>
			: 
				Sup.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡβάσεις ἥβαν ἀνοστοτάταν</span>”
				<i>never, never to return,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					AP
					7.482
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			= foreg. <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				4.13.2
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			).</div>
